WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.160
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:06.430 --> 00:08.029
Chemi, could you take this, please?

3
00:08.029 --> 00:09.830
I spent all night writing it.

4
00:09.830 --> 00:10.930
I want you to read it.

5
00:11.500 --> 00:12.300
Okay.

6
00:12.770 --> 00:15.430
I'm not sure you won't hurt my brother again.

7
00:15.430 --> 00:17.300
Do I really look that bad to you?

8
00:19.400 --> 00:21.900
He's not picking up. I've called ten times.

9
00:27.070 --> 00:28.000
I'm his brother.

10
00:28.930 --> 00:30.430
I have a right to worry.

11
00:30.430 --> 00:33.930
If you want me in it, you have to cast someone close to me too.

12
00:33.930 --> 00:36.030
Your co-star is Din.

13
00:39.870 --> 00:41.770
Go tell him now. I'll be your co-star.

14
00:41.770 --> 00:42.700
Bro...

15
00:43.000 --> 00:44.500
I'll give you another chance.

16
00:46.370 --> 00:47.930
It's only been one day.

17
00:49.100 --> 00:50.800
I waited four years for you.

18
00:51.600 --> 00:53.370
Take good care of me.

19
00:53.930 --> 00:56.530
I know what you're thinking, Rei.

20
00:57.000 --> 00:59.700
But you're really just a big brother to me.

21
00:59.700 --> 01:00.630
I get it.

22
01:00.930 --> 01:01.900
I'll head home.

23
01:01.900 --> 01:03.130
Din,

24
01:03.500 --> 01:04.900
I have feelings for you.

25
01:04.900 --> 01:07.030
I have feelings for you too.

26
01:08.000 --> 01:09.800
I love doing nice things for you.

27
01:09.800 --> 01:11.600
Keep up the quality, okay?

28
01:12.130 --> 01:12.930
Hello, Mii.

29
01:14.030 --> 01:15.170
Come out and see me.

30
01:16.370 --> 01:17.470
I need to talk to you.

31
01:40.930 --> 01:42.400
So what now, Mii?

32
01:42.400 --> 01:44.470
Do you know who Rei's hitting on now?

33
01:44.470 --> 01:47.570
He's hitting on everyone. Get a grip, Mii.

34
02:00.270 --> 02:01.970
Why'd you call me here, Aof?

35
02:07.170 --> 02:08.770
If you won't talk, I'm leaving.

36
02:11.600 --> 02:12.830
It's about Rei.

37
02:14.400 --> 02:16.570
Rei's been hitting on a junior at my school.

38
02:18.800 --> 02:21.000
But he doesn't seem interested.

39
02:21.000 --> 02:23.500
Tomorrow at school, I'll talk to him for you.

40
02:23.500 --> 02:25.600
And I'll let you know what I find out.

41
02:29.530 --> 02:30.370
Mii.

42
02:31.200 --> 02:32.730
Mii, just break up with Rei.

43
02:35.630 --> 02:37.370
Don't put up with a guy like him.

44
02:40.400 --> 02:42.530
I'm going to break up with him, but...

45
02:42.530 --> 02:45.530
Just one last time. Really, just once.

46
02:45.530 --> 02:47.030
Mii, how many times now?

47
02:50.600 --> 02:53.230
I'm saying this because I care about you, Mii.

48
04:57.830 --> 04:59.300
Didn't I ask you before?

49
04:59.300 --> 05:01.800
If you didn't love me, just break up with me.

50
05:01.800 --> 05:02.900
Be straight with me.

51
05:02.900 --> 05:04.230
And you cheated on me.

52
05:04.230 --> 05:05.370
How could you do this?

53
05:10.100 --> 05:13.070
Answer me! Say something!

54
05:13.070 --> 05:14.500
Answer me, Rei!

55
05:18.200 --> 05:19.630
I'm sorry.

56
05:20.700 --> 05:22.700
But I'm the one who hurt you.

57
05:24.330 --> 05:25.630
So you choose.

58
05:26.230 --> 05:27.330
What's it going to be?

59
05:38.700 --> 05:39.830
Disgusting.

60
05:41.530 --> 05:43.500
You know you're a total scumbag?

61
05:43.500 --> 05:46.970
You come into my life, cheat on me, and then tell me to choose?

62
05:47.770 --> 05:49.900
Why didn't you just break up with me?

63
05:51.330 --> 05:52.130
Huh?!

64
05:55.870 --> 05:57.130
Scared?

65
06:06.670 --> 06:09.470
I hope I never have to see your face again.

66
06:47.970 --> 06:49.130
Hey, Star.

67
06:49.730 --> 06:51.030
We're out of staples.

68
06:51.030 --> 06:53.800
We need to buy more or we won't finish today.

69
06:53.800 --> 06:55.400
Yeah, wanna go buy some?

70
06:56.270 --> 07:01.430
Or how about we borrow staples from the guys building the stage set?

71
07:04.870 --> 07:07.500
Hm, you really want to go?

72
07:07.500 --> 07:09.500
Fine, let's go together.

73
07:10.870 --> 07:13.370
I doubt it's just about the staples.

74
07:14.030 --> 07:17.030
From the looks of it, you just want to see Din, right?

75
07:19.830 --> 07:22.030
Go, go. Get there and back fast.

76
07:22.030 --> 07:23.570
Fine, I'll go. I'll go.

77
07:33.600 --> 07:35.930
Uh, the popcorn cart goes at Booth One.

78
07:35.930 --> 07:37.370
Careful setting it up.

79
07:58.230 --> 08:00.870
I brought you pink milk. Your favorite.

80
08:03.530 --> 08:06.070
The event's coming up. We won't make it in time.

81
08:06.400 --> 08:09.500
Hey, trust me. We'll make it. You've got me.

82
08:17.400 --> 08:19.900
It's going slow because you keep fussing over me.

83
08:20.700 --> 08:23.470
Oh, come on. Here, have a drink. Go on, take a break.

84
08:36.100 --> 08:37.070
Action!

85
08:48.200 --> 08:50.470
Why do you follow me so?

86
08:51.970 --> 08:53.700
For I caught a god's scent.

87
08:53.700 --> 08:55.130
Well, I am a god.

88
08:59.170 --> 09:02.230
My lord, I have a question.

89
09:03.500 --> 09:07.200
Just now, I saw two humans touch their mouths together.

90
09:07.200 --> 09:08.570
What was that, my lord?

91
09:10.200 --> 09:13.670
It is one way humans show love.

92
09:13.670 --> 09:16.070
If one day you love someone dearly,

93
09:17.100 --> 09:19.930
you may show it in the same way.

94
09:21.170 --> 09:23.370
On to the kiss scene. Action!

95
09:48.800 --> 09:53.070
My lord, then I...

96
10:03.100 --> 10:05.100
I don't think we need to really kiss.

97
10:05.100 --> 10:06.970
Is there another way?

98
10:06.970 --> 10:08.430
I don't want to actually kiss.

99
10:11.000 --> 10:14.100
I don't think it'll look convincing.

100
10:14.100 --> 10:16.100
Because in a stage play,

101
10:16.100 --> 10:17.970
the audience sees from every angle.

102
10:18.400 --> 10:21.400
It's not like film or TV, where camera angles can fake it.

103
10:22.200 --> 10:23.000
Hmm.

104
10:23.000 --> 10:25.000
I agree with Kim.

105
10:25.670 --> 10:26.670
Honestly...

106
10:26.670 --> 10:29.330
We all want this to be the best it can be, right?

107
10:30.000 --> 10:31.230
Right, Fuen?

108
10:32.970 --> 10:34.700
If Fuen and Din agree,

109
10:36.870 --> 10:38.070
as actors,

110
10:38.930 --> 10:41.230
they should give it their all, right?

111
10:43.870 --> 10:45.630
And me, as the audience?

112
10:46.300 --> 10:47.670
I'm totally fine with it.

113
10:53.900 --> 10:56.200
Go into the kiss scene. Action!

114
10:58.400 --> 10:59.300
Din.

115
11:00.730 --> 11:02.100
Kiss for real.

116
11:03.470 --> 11:05.330
Mm, okay.

117
11:18.770 --> 11:21.630
My lord, then I...

118
11:30.900 --> 11:32.100
Din!

119
11:44.770 --> 11:47.070
Can I borrow the stapler?

120
11:47.930 --> 11:49.270
Sure.

121
11:56.600 --> 12:00.470
Star!

122
12:03.300 --> 12:04.500
Dude.

123
12:05.030 --> 12:08.270
It's fine. We haven't finished rehearsing.

124
12:11.770 --> 12:13.830
Let's finish rehearsing first.

125
12:17.600 --> 12:21.930
Oh, hey, we've all been rehearsing for a while now.

126
12:21.930 --> 12:23.230
Is everyone hungry?

127
12:23.470 --> 12:25.200
Hungry? Anyone hungry?

128
12:25.530 --> 12:26.430
Yes, starving!

129
12:26.770 --> 12:27.600
Then...

130
12:27.600 --> 12:28.630
Hey, I think...

131
12:29.470 --> 12:30.500
Mm.

132
12:31.770 --> 12:34.330
We've been rehearsing for hours, Kim.

133
12:34.770 --> 12:37.470
I think we should take a little break.

134
12:38.830 --> 12:39.830
Okay.

135
12:39.830 --> 12:40.930
Let's eat, then.

136
12:42.670 --> 12:43.500
Okay.

137
12:44.270 --> 12:45.030
Tell them, then.

138
12:46.070 --> 12:47.730
Okay, everyone, time to eat!

139
12:47.730 --> 12:49.300
Go on, go eat, guys.

140
12:50.100 --> 12:50.730
Okay, okay.

141
12:50.730 --> 12:52.530
Wow, great job! Awesome!

142
12:52.530 --> 12:53.600
Thanks, man.

143
13:04.530 --> 13:06.730
Star, wait! Wait, Star!

144
13:07.270 --> 13:08.330
Are you okay?

145
13:12.830 --> 13:15.670
Booboo, I shouldn't have walked off like that.

146
13:16.030 --> 13:18.830
Din was just rehearsing. Or am I being silly?

147
13:19.170 --> 13:20.970
Hey, no. / You're fine.

148
13:20.970 --> 13:24.330
It's normal to feel that. Din didn't tell you first, right?

149
13:24.900 --> 13:28.070
True. If you'd known beforehand, this wouldn't have happened.

150
13:28.070 --> 13:30.030
That was one hell of a surprise.

151
13:30.900 --> 13:32.070
It's fine, guys.

152
13:32.070 --> 13:35.200
Or should I just go back to Din?

153
13:35.770 --> 13:37.130
Mm, good idea.

154
13:48.800 --> 13:50.570
Can I talk to you for a bit?

155
14:14.030 --> 14:15.300
What?

156
14:15.870 --> 14:17.200
I'm okay with it.

157
14:17.200 --> 14:18.230
Let's go all in.

158
14:18.430 --> 14:19.470
You sure?

159
14:21.130 --> 14:21.830
Mm.

160
14:27.830 --> 14:28.800
I'm sure.

161
14:35.500 --> 14:36.770
Acting.

162
14:41.000 --> 14:42.470
Let's just call it acting.

163
14:42.830 --> 14:43.630
Mm.

164
14:44.570 --> 14:46.600
Of course it's acting.

165
15:00.130 --> 15:01.600
Din.

166
15:02.170 --> 15:04.900
I'm sorry for walking out like that.

167
15:06.430 --> 15:08.300
Did I make you feel bad?

168
15:08.700 --> 15:10.000
Not at all.

169
15:10.470 --> 15:12.500
I was more worried you'd get the wrong idea.

170
15:14.200 --> 15:18.570
Fuen and I are really just following the script. There's nothing more to it.

171
15:19.500 --> 15:20.900
I understand.

172
15:21.600 --> 15:24.230
So don't worry about me, okay?

173
15:24.230 --> 15:26.230
Go back to your rehearsal.

174
15:27.000 --> 15:29.930
You're sure you're really okay?

175
15:34.000 --> 15:35.670
I'm sure.

176
15:37.530 --> 15:41.030
Then on the day, save me a seat, okay?

177
15:41.670 --> 15:43.670
I want to see you show off your acting.

178
15:45.970 --> 15:50.670
And... when it comes to that scene...

179
15:51.470 --> 15:55.100
Just a peck. Nothing more.

180
15:55.530 --> 15:57.970
Okay. Just a little peck.

181
16:09.270 --> 16:10.770
Our friends are adorable.

182
16:10.770 --> 16:12.830
We should cast them all in the play.

183
16:15.330 --> 16:16.830
Right. / Right.

184
16:18.970 --> 16:21.500
Star, I need to talk to you.

185
16:21.500 --> 16:23.070
What do you want with Star?

186
16:23.070 --> 16:24.730
I'm talking to him. Stay out of it.

187
16:27.900 --> 16:30.230
It is my business. I'm trying to win Star over.

188
16:30.570 --> 16:31.600
What?!

189
16:40.630 --> 16:42.070
Shit.

190
16:42.070 --> 16:43.700
Where the hell do I even start?

191
16:44.130 --> 16:46.230
Star, I'll get straight to the point.

192
16:46.230 --> 16:48.070
I've never thought badly of you.

193
16:49.270 --> 16:51.130
But what's going on with you and Rei?

194
17:03.970 --> 17:06.069
Rei and I really aren't anything.

195
17:07.170 --> 17:08.930
I don't even like him.

196
17:08.930 --> 17:11.099
But yesterday at Siam, I saw you hugging him.

197
17:20.329 --> 17:24.329
Aof, that thing at Siam was just an accident.

198
17:24.329 --> 17:27.970
Rei was just catching me. I was about to fall.

199
17:39.770 --> 17:41.970
Is there something I should know?

200
17:42.530 --> 17:43.930
It's a long story.

201
17:44.270 --> 17:45.400
It's about Mii.

202
17:46.370 --> 17:47.730
I'm not sure about Rei.

203
17:47.730 --> 17:49.530
So I came to check with Star.

204
17:49.930 --> 17:52.470
I knew it. Star wouldn't go for a guy like that.

205
17:53.900 --> 17:55.730
I'm so damn worried about Mii.

206
17:55.930 --> 17:58.430
No idea how she's doing. She won't answer my calls.

207
18:06.330 --> 18:08.000
You're sure it was just an accident?

208
18:09.430 --> 18:10.600
Yes.

209
18:50.570 --> 18:51.570
Hello, Aof.

210
18:52.000 --> 18:54.270
Hello, Mii. How are you?

211
18:55.700 --> 18:59.970
I'm okay, I guess. I broke up with him.

212
19:01.400 --> 19:04.070
I don't know how I put up with him for so long.

213
19:06.130 --> 19:07.570
I feel so relieved now.

214
19:09.070 --> 19:14.170
Mm, good. If anything's bothering you, just tell me.

215
19:17.570 --> 19:18.370
Mm.

216
19:18.800 --> 19:21.070
I'm with a lot of friends right now.

217
19:21.530 --> 19:22.670
It's fine.

218
19:23.570 --> 19:26.170
But if I really can't take it,

219
19:26.900 --> 19:28.670
can you pull me back, Aof?

220
19:31.430 --> 19:32.330
Of course.

221
19:33.200 --> 19:34.630
Thanks.

222
19:35.270 --> 19:36.970
Mii, let's go to Siam.

223
19:37.730 --> 19:40.600
Aof, I'll go now. Heading to Siam. Bye.

224
19:40.600 --> 19:42.000
You take care too, Mii.

225
19:42.570 --> 19:44.670
Message me anytime if anything comes up.

226
20:02.770 --> 20:04.230
You're sure about this setlist?

227
20:08.030 --> 20:13.070
I was thinking, if we swap this song with this one,

228
20:13.070 --> 20:16.130
it might open better, and feel fresh for everyone.

229
20:16.700 --> 20:17.730
What do you think?

230
20:18.670 --> 20:20.900
Shall we try running it once?

231
20:21.400 --> 20:23.200
Sure. / Let's see if it works.

232
20:23.200 --> 20:24.500
Okay, everyone, places.

233
20:34.600 --> 20:40.430
♪ Have you ever felt it — no matter how far the days carry us ♪

234
20:40.430 --> 20:44.370
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, on the story of that day ♪

235
20:44.370 --> 20:50.800
♪ it warms my heart all over again ♪

236
20:52.030 --> 20:58.030
♪ Looking at the photos some nights before I sleep, I smile to myself ♪

237
20:58.030 --> 21:01.700
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, on you and me ♪

238
21:01.700 --> 21:06.430
♪ a time I've never once forgotten ♪

239
21:09.630 --> 21:16.370
♪ However long the years run on, my heart still won't forget ♪

240
21:18.130 --> 21:25.370
♪ Even if we had to part in the end, that time is still just as it was ♪

241
21:25.370 --> 21:29.270
♪ It's all still so clear inside me ♪

242
21:29.270 --> 21:33.570
♪ I still remember all our good times, just the same ♪

243
21:33.570 --> 21:37.770
♪ The days we smiled at each other, the days we were close ♪

244
21:37.770 --> 21:42.630
♪ None of it has ever gone away ♪

245
21:42.630 --> 21:46.630
♪ It's all still so clear, it never faded ♪

246
21:46.630 --> 21:50.800
♪ Even if today we have to go our separate ways ♪

247
21:50.800 --> 21:55.370
♪ However far apart you and I may be ♪

248
21:55.370 --> 21:59.930
♪ our time together is still here in my heart ♪

249
21:59.930 --> 22:03.200
♪ It's all still so clear ♪

250
22:09.530 --> 22:12.930
Thank you so much to the crew and everyone today.

251
22:12.930 --> 22:16.730
That's a wrap for today. And don't forget to study your lines.

252
22:22.130 --> 22:24.930
Stage crew, you can bring the set up now.

253
22:33.430 --> 22:35.330
How you doing? / Nervous, obviously.

254
22:36.300 --> 22:37.500
You okay?

255
22:37.970 --> 22:39.970
Go home and get some rest.

256
22:42.170 --> 22:43.200
Hey!

257
22:47.630 --> 22:49.330
Hey! Get over here, quick!

258
22:50.800 --> 22:51.830
Are you okay?

259
22:53.070 --> 22:53.930
You alright?

260
22:53.930 --> 22:54.700
Physics!

261
22:57.800 --> 22:58.870
Easy, get up slowly.

262
23:00.370 --> 23:01.400
Are you hurt?

263
23:01.400 --> 23:02.570
No, no, it's nothing.

264
23:02.570 --> 23:04.070
I'm okay. It's fine, it's fine.

265
23:04.470 --> 23:05.330
Let me see.

266
23:05.930 --> 23:06.870
Ow! / Oops!

267
23:07.300 --> 23:08.370
Fine? Seriously?

268
23:08.370 --> 23:10.170
Come on, to the nurse's office.

269
23:12.370 --> 23:13.370
I'm so sorry.

270
23:14.300 --> 23:15.300
It's okay.

271
23:17.470 --> 23:19.400
You guys need to be more careful!

272
23:24.130 --> 23:25.400
Let's go.

273
23:26.730 --> 23:28.270
I'll walk you there.

274
23:34.300 --> 23:35.130
Goodbye.

275
23:35.130 --> 23:37.200
Bye! Bye!

276
23:37.530 --> 23:39.300
Bye! Get home safe!

277
23:42.200 --> 23:43.230
Chemi.

278
23:44.330 --> 23:45.600
Oh, Aof.

279
23:46.230 --> 23:48.170
Every song you sang was great.

280
23:49.500 --> 23:51.330
I got totally lost listening.

281
24:16.370 --> 24:17.800
Why didn't you say you'd come?

282
24:18.770 --> 24:20.430
Have you been waiting long?

283
24:21.500 --> 24:22.530
Not long.

284
24:23.670 --> 24:25.730
I still want to hear you sing.

285
24:26.770 --> 24:28.330
Will you sing more for me?

286
24:28.330 --> 24:29.270
Hm?

287
24:31.300 --> 24:35.030
Sing here? There are so many people around.

288
24:36.770 --> 24:39.800
But... next time I come to sing again,

289
24:40.700 --> 24:42.430
I'll sing for you, okay?

290
24:43.600 --> 24:46.070
I knew you'd say that to me.

291
24:46.070 --> 24:47.670
Good thing I came prepared.

292
24:48.930 --> 24:50.400
I recorded every song.

293
24:55.400 --> 24:59.470
Ugh, that's embarrassing.

294
25:04.230 --> 25:07.970
So how was rehearsal today? Tired?

295
25:10.030 --> 25:12.370
Will you change on me, Aof?

296
25:16.570 --> 25:18.630
Are you only being nice to me for now?

297
25:19.430 --> 25:22.030
I get it if that's what you think.

298
25:22.800 --> 25:24.370
But this time,

299
25:25.370 --> 25:28.570
you don't have to believe my words, Chemi.

300
25:31.870 --> 25:33.670
Just watch what I do.

301
25:38.000 --> 25:40.230
I'll be watching closely.

302
25:45.970 --> 25:47.300
So how was today?

303
25:47.300 --> 25:48.300
Was rehearsal tiring?

304
25:48.900 --> 25:53.630
Not tiring at all. It was so fun. And most of all,

305
25:54.670 --> 25:57.330
Thanop helped me out a lot.

306
25:59.230 --> 26:01.830
There were things I didn't even know I was doing wrong,

307
26:01.830 --> 26:03.300
and he helped me fix them.

308
26:06.370 --> 26:11.600
I'm serious about this. Why not think about switching clubs?

309
26:12.430 --> 26:16.800
If you get to do what you love, I think you'll be happier.

310
26:27.870 --> 26:29.430
But taking care of you...

311
26:29.430 --> 26:31.130
makes me happy too.

312
26:45.630 --> 26:47.370
But I'll think about it.

313
26:49.000 --> 26:52.570
Maybe I'll do both clubs, like Thanop.

314
26:54.330 --> 26:55.370
Chemi.

315
26:55.700 --> 26:57.000
I'm dead serious.

316
26:57.000 --> 26:58.100
What is it?

317
26:58.100 --> 27:00.170
Can you stop talking about Thanop?

318
27:01.100 --> 27:03.970
I know he's good at football,

319
27:03.970 --> 27:07.030
he plays music, and he's damn smart.

320
27:07.400 --> 27:11.500
On top of that, he's a good guy. And most of all, he's handsome too.

321
27:13.100 --> 27:17.770
But everything I just said, I can do too.

322
27:20.230 --> 27:23.430
Yes, you're the best.

323
27:28.130 --> 27:29.270
Fabulous.

324
27:34.270 --> 27:38.500
Come on, let's go home. I'll take you today.

325
27:40.830 --> 27:41.770
Okay.

326
28:00.600 --> 28:02.000
Easy, walk slowly. Easy.

327
28:02.270 --> 28:03.070
Ow.

328
28:03.070 --> 28:04.430
Easy, easy, easy.

329
28:04.430 --> 28:06.130
Hold on, hold on. Wait for me.

330
28:10.070 --> 28:11.600
Owww.

331
28:11.600 --> 28:14.270
Not the arm! It hurts! / Sorry, sorry.

332
28:17.830 --> 28:19.270
Lucky you can still walk.

333
28:20.130 --> 28:21.470
It's fine.

334
28:22.500 --> 28:23.430
Hey.

335
28:23.430 --> 28:24.400
Hm?

336
28:24.800 --> 28:26.830
Thanks a lot for today.

337
28:27.830 --> 28:30.230
No problem. It's nothing.

338
28:32.930 --> 28:37.830
From now on, I'll take care of you.

339
28:43.400 --> 28:45.400
Let me put the bag away first.

340
28:47.100 --> 28:48.300
Hey!

341
29:03.800 --> 29:05.630
You said you'd take care of me, right?

342
29:08.070 --> 29:09.000
Bathe me, then.

343
29:09.000 --> 29:09.670
What?!

344
29:09.670 --> 29:11.400
I'm all sticky.

345
29:11.830 --> 29:13.500
Don't you have another arm?

346
29:14.830 --> 29:16.630
That arm hurts too.

347
29:20.030 --> 29:21.070
Then...

348
29:23.900 --> 29:25.630
Just wash my hair, please?

349
29:30.930 --> 29:32.170
Okay.

350
29:33.630 --> 29:38.200
Hair wash. / Hair wash. Mm.

351
30:05.030 --> 30:06.530
Lots of it.

352
30:07.270 --> 30:08.430
Go for it.

353
30:12.600 --> 30:13.900
Scrub it all out.

354
30:13.900 --> 30:14.930
This feels so good.

355
30:14.930 --> 30:15.730
Mm.

356
30:17.700 --> 30:18.870
Mind your eyes.

357
30:19.500 --> 30:22.730
Then don't move so much or the foam'll get in your eyes.

358
30:23.170 --> 30:26.270
Hey, I just remembered. I've got a toy.

359
30:26.270 --> 30:27.100
What is it?

360
30:32.660 --> 30:36.560
♪ It's all still so clear inside me ♪

361
30:36.560 --> 30:40.860
♪ I still remember all our good times, just the same ♪

362
30:40.860 --> 30:45.060
♪ The days we smiled at each other, the days we were close ♪

363
30:45.060 --> 30:49.920
♪ None of it has ever gone away ♪

364
30:49.920 --> 30:53.920
♪ It's all still so clear, it never faded ♪

365
30:53.920 --> 30:58.090
♪ Even if today we have to go our separate ways ♪

366
30:58.090 --> 31:02.660
♪ However far apart you and I may be ♪

367
31:02.660 --> 31:07.220
♪ our time together is still here in my heart ♪

368
31:07.220 --> 31:10.490
♪ It's all still so clear ♪

369
31:21.130 --> 31:22.470
Who's that?

370
31:22.470 --> 31:24.230
Hm? / Who is it?

371
31:24.230 --> 31:27.930
Oh, nobody. Just a general notification.

372
31:28.570 --> 31:30.800
And I thought nobody ever texts you.

373
31:37.100 --> 31:38.900
Close your eyes or it'll get in them.

374
31:58.330 --> 31:59.700
Guys!

375
32:02.930 --> 32:05.300
The tickets are sold out!

376
33:12.230 --> 33:13.870
Amazing! Amazing!

377
34:25.929 --> 34:26.929
Chemi.

378
34:29.770 --> 34:31.370
Yes, what can I get you?

379
34:31.900 --> 34:32.900
Give me a sec.

380
34:37.100 --> 34:38.270
Let me help.

381
34:39.630 --> 34:42.699
Do you know how? You won't wreck my shop?

382
34:42.699 --> 34:45.600
I thought you only knew how to use your feet.

383
34:45.600 --> 34:47.230
You underestimate me way too much.

384
34:47.230 --> 34:49.130
Just watch me.

385
34:56.600 --> 34:58.200
Excuse me!

386
34:58.200 --> 35:00.570
Your watermelon smoothies are ready.

387
35:11.370 --> 35:13.730
But this shop's watermelon smoothies...

388
35:13.730 --> 35:15.030
are for sale only.

389
35:15.030 --> 35:17.730
No flirting. The seller's already taken.

390
35:29.070 --> 35:30.570
Here you go.

391
35:41.800 --> 35:46.100
Everyone, come see FUN VIBE tonight. There's a concert.

392
36:06.430 --> 36:09.670
Welcome to the 5/1 Escape Room.

393
36:23.630 --> 36:27.400
This round is Tang's turn.

394
36:28.600 --> 36:30.800
Whoa, I'm playing alone?

395
36:31.270 --> 36:33.530
Time invited me, so he's playing with me.

396
36:34.970 --> 36:39.370
Then this round is Tang and Time's.

397
36:43.570 --> 36:44.700
Go ahead.

398
37:02.030 --> 37:05.470
Hey, didn't you make this room? Why are you more scared than me?

399
37:05.470 --> 37:09.300
I just cut paper and sewed. I didn't think my friends made it this scary.

400
37:10.830 --> 37:12.770
So how does this work?

401
37:16.700 --> 37:18.670
You just answer the questions in time.

402
37:19.570 --> 37:20.370
Answer questions.

403
37:21.370 --> 37:22.970
In here? / Mm-hmm.

404
37:22.970 --> 37:24.330
The clock's running.

405
37:25.170 --> 37:28.870
What lives on the ground all the time, but never gets dirty?

406
37:31.000 --> 37:32.900
Aren't you smart? Answer it.

407
37:33.330 --> 37:34.430
Help me think.

408
37:34.430 --> 37:35.670
I don't know.

409
37:35.670 --> 37:37.900
And what happens if you don't answer in time?

410
37:37.900 --> 37:38.970
You'll find out.

411
37:41.000 --> 37:42.100
Whoa!

412
37:45.100 --> 37:47.670
Lives on the ground all the time, but isn't dirty.

413
37:48.570 --> 37:50.130
Uh, I don't know.

414
37:50.900 --> 37:51.770
A worm?

415
37:52.670 --> 37:54.300
No, that's wrong.

416
37:56.030 --> 37:57.070
A mole?

417
37:57.070 --> 37:57.870
What mole?

418
37:58.970 --> 38:00.500
Lives on the ground...

419
38:00.500 --> 38:02.700
Hurry! Solve the riddle to get out!

420
38:03.000 --> 38:03.970
but isn't dirty.

421
38:04.130 --> 38:06.300
No, wrong. / I don't know!

422
38:06.800 --> 38:07.700
Is it an animal?

423
38:08.170 --> 38:10.270
I don't know. It must say in there.

424
38:11.000 --> 38:13.170
Lives on the ground, but never gets dir...

425
38:13.170 --> 38:14.270
Whoa!!!

426
38:21.970 --> 38:26.300
Hello! The day you've all been waiting for is here.

427
38:26.300 --> 38:29.930
This is just one part of the Thapfah Open House.

428
38:29.930 --> 38:34.270
I promise this event will be fun and over the top.

429
38:34.270 --> 38:36.670
If you've got tickets, hurry on down.

430
38:36.670 --> 38:39.970
If you don't have one yet, you can buy one at the door.

431
38:39.970 --> 38:41.730
But there aren't many left.

432
38:41.730 --> 38:43.700
Hurry over, everyone!

433
38:43.700 --> 38:50.070
And lots of people have been asking about confessing your love at the last firework,

434
38:50.070 --> 38:53.030
the legend of Thapfah Wittayanusorn School.

435
38:53.300 --> 38:55.970
Come on, I'll tell you all about it.

436
38:59.270 --> 39:05.530
Once upon a time, Lord Thapfah was a king known for his fairness,

437
39:05.530 --> 39:08.000
and much beloved by his people.

438
39:08.500 --> 39:12.670
One day, while he was out traveling as usual,

439
39:12.670 --> 39:16.930
he came across a white monkey shaped like a man,

440
39:16.930 --> 39:20.000
who seemed clever and could speak human language.

441
39:21.600 --> 39:24.770
Intrigued, the king brought him home.

442
39:39.570 --> 39:44.070
After that, the white monkey followed the king everywhere.

443
39:45.400 --> 39:48.200
He mastered the use of weapons,

444
39:48.200 --> 39:51.830
until he became one of the king's top guards.

445
40:05.700 --> 40:10.170
But then one day, the white monkey had a thought.

446
40:10.170 --> 40:12.770
He didn't want Lord Thapfah to be with anyone else.

447
40:12.770 --> 40:19.570
And he was jealous, knowing the king had to marry according to tradition.

448
40:39.800 --> 40:44.200
So the white monkey decided to confess his feelings.

449
40:44.200 --> 40:48.700
And that was the first time Lord Thapfah ever shed tears,

450
40:48.700 --> 40:52.370
because it was forbidden, the one thing that must never happen.

451
41:00.230 --> 41:03.030
And even though he felt the same,

452
41:03.030 --> 41:06.700
the two of them could not be together.

453
41:06.700 --> 41:09.400
The white monkey listened and understood,

454
41:09.400 --> 41:11.830
but could not stop loving him.

455
41:12.400 --> 41:18.630
So he swore an oath to love and honor the king forever.

456
41:19.500 --> 41:24.400
And at that very moment, as if his love had been blessed,

457
41:24.400 --> 41:28.900
ten shooting stars suddenly appeared in the sky.

458
41:28.900 --> 41:32.730
And the last one was the moment they confessed their love.

459
41:32.730 --> 41:36.100
That's how our school's legend came to be:

460
41:36.100 --> 41:42.030
if two people truly confess their love as the last firework is launched into the sky,

461
41:42.030 --> 41:47.170
they'll be blessed by the sacred spirits, just as they once were.

462
41:50.570 --> 41:53.200
You think that legend's true?

463
41:53.200 --> 41:54.870
No idea, but I want to try.

464
41:55.400 --> 41:58.770
Chemi, let's watch the fireworks this evening.

465
41:58.770 --> 42:01.600
Wait for me in front of the room. I'll come find you.

466
42:04.670 --> 42:08.530
The play was so fun. Thanks for inviting me.

467
42:08.530 --> 42:10.330
I asked you here for the fireworks.

468
42:56.270 --> 42:57.400
Great job.

469
43:06.970 --> 43:08.570
This is for you, Din.

470
43:09.930 --> 43:11.070
Thank you.

471
43:16.900 --> 43:19.730
Star, stay and watch the fireworks with me tonight.

472
43:22.100 --> 43:23.400
Okay.

473
43:25.270 --> 43:28.300
Then can I take a picture with the monkey?

474
44:15.230 --> 44:20.130
♪ There's something in my heart I can't explain ♪

475
44:20.130 --> 44:24.270
♪ Still searching for someone to tell me ♪

476
44:24.270 --> 44:27.600
♪ No matter how much time goes by ♪

477
44:27.600 --> 44:29.970
♪ I never find what I'm looking for ♪

478
44:29.970 --> 44:34.100
♪ Why does my heart still feel so empty? ♪

479
44:34.100 --> 44:38.130
♪ I want to think it through, to find an answer ♪

480
44:38.130 --> 44:42.330
♪ To these feelings I can't read ♪

481
44:42.330 --> 44:45.970
♪ No matter how much time goes by ♪

482
44:45.970 --> 44:48.170
♪ I still want to know ♪

483
44:48.170 --> 44:52.670
♪ is there someone who can help me? ♪

484
44:52.670 --> 44:56.870
♪ Then you came along, and everything changed ♪

485
44:56.870 --> 45:01.330
♪ What was blurred before began to sharpen inside me ♪

486
45:01.330 --> 45:05.970
♪ I never knew who I was waiting for ♪

487
45:05.970 --> 45:09.970
♪ until you came, and today I understand ♪

488
45:09.970 --> 45:14.270
♪ Because of you I know what I was waiting for ♪

489
45:14.270 --> 45:19.570
♪ The nights that were empty now mean something ♪

490
45:19.570 --> 45:24.930
♪ Every question in my heart has an answer now ♪

491
45:24.930 --> 45:30.170
♪ You're the one who made me understand — in the end, the answer is you ♪

492
45:34.300 --> 45:37.670
♪ From that day, the day we met, my heart was never the same ♪

493
45:37.670 --> 45:39.030
That's my brother! My brother!

494
45:39.030 --> 45:40.530
Yeah, I know.

495
45:51.170 --> 45:52.430
Hello?

496
45:54.770 --> 45:56.070
Say that again?

497
45:56.530 --> 45:57.830
You're here?

498
45:58.800 --> 46:00.330
Okay, okay.

499
46:06.930 --> 46:08.370
I'll be right back.

500
46:08.930 --> 46:10.330
Be right back. / Mm.

501
46:10.770 --> 46:11.970
A friend just showed up.

502
46:13.230 --> 46:14.930
I'll join you for the fireworks.

503
46:14.930 --> 46:16.970
Ah, okay. Go.

504
46:16.970 --> 46:18.770
There's still plenty of time.

505
46:19.370 --> 46:22.000
I'll be quick and hurry back to you.

506
46:23.700 --> 46:25.470
I want to watch the fireworks with you.

507
46:27.170 --> 46:28.400
I'm not going anywhere.

508
46:29.730 --> 46:34.300
♪ showed someone who was lost the way to his own heart ♪

509
46:34.300 --> 46:36.900
♪ everything I'd been searching for ♪

510
46:36.900 --> 46:42.400
♪ Every question in my heart has an answer now ♪

511
46:42.400 --> 46:44.770
♪ Whatever the story turns out to be ♪

512
46:44.770 --> 46:47.800
♪ in the end, my answer is you ♪

513
47:03.530 --> 47:06.730
♪ Because of you, a world that was all noise ♪

514
47:06.730 --> 47:13.700
♪ showed someone who was lost the way to his own heart, everything I'd been searching for ♪

515
47:13.700 --> 47:18.930
♪ Every question in my heart has an answer now ♪

516
47:18.930 --> 47:24.970
♪ No matter how the story goes, in the end my answer is you ♪

517
47:41.730 --> 47:42.930
I'll be right back.

518
47:56.330 --> 47:58.200
"I'm here."

519
48:09.500 --> 48:13.070
Alright, everyone, we'll take a short break.

520
48:13.070 --> 48:18.970
Because the big moment you've all been waiting for has arrived.

521
48:19.870 --> 48:22.800
Let's go watch the fireworks!

522
48:49.030 --> 48:50.830
Ten

523
48:57.930 --> 48:59.730
Nine

524
49:04.670 --> 49:06.470
Eight

525
49:10.630 --> 49:12.430
Seven

526
49:15.630 --> 49:17.430
Six

527
49:25.200 --> 49:27.000
Five

528
49:45.030 --> 49:48.430
Tang, let's take a picture.

529
50:11.130 --> 50:12.870
Din.

530
50:13.570 --> 50:16.930
Can I borrow your phone for a sec?

531
50:27.000 --> 50:28.430
Thank you.

532
50:30.480 --> 50:33.360
"Requested"

533
50:36.800 --> 50:41.000
If we talk in here, it's not cheating, right?

534
50:41.000 --> 50:44.400
Because we're talking through pictures.

535
50:44.400 --> 50:48.230
So you have to post pictures often, okay?

536
50:48.630 --> 50:50.000
You got it.

537
50:51.330 --> 50:54.170
Then I'll post often too.

538
51:10.670 --> 51:13.500
I know you take good care of yourself, Time,

539
51:15.000 --> 51:17.170
but let me take even better care of you.

540
51:38.670 --> 51:40.330
Glad you came, man.

541
51:40.330 --> 51:41.900
Missed you like crazy.

542
51:42.370 --> 51:45.030
But I've got to go now.

543
51:45.570 --> 51:48.630
You got ICL's offer. What are you waiting for?

544
51:48.630 --> 51:50.300
Isn't that your dream university?

545
51:50.300 --> 51:53.000
And besides, even if I study in Bournemouth,

546
51:53.000 --> 51:55.200
it's only two hours from London.

547
51:55.200 --> 51:56.600
I can come see you.

548
52:14.100 --> 52:15.070
What do I do?

549
52:15.500 --> 52:19.230
Honestly, that's not what's holding me back.

550
52:20.600 --> 52:22.970
But I've got something to deal with here first.

551
52:25.170 --> 52:26.330
I'm off.

552
52:32.870 --> 52:33.900
Fuen!

553
52:38.500 --> 52:39.400
Fuen!

554
52:39.400 --> 52:40.030
Physics.

555
52:40.030 --> 52:41.030
Fuen.

556
52:45.200 --> 52:46.200
Fuen.

557
52:46.800 --> 52:47.800
Fuen, wait.

558
52:52.130 --> 52:54.530
Fuen, listen to me first.

559
52:55.630 --> 52:57.900
Why didn't you ever think to tell me?

560
52:58.530 --> 53:01.030
You're with me almost all the time.

561
53:02.930 --> 53:04.670
And you never thought to tell me.

562
53:08.000 --> 53:10.170
What am I to you, Physics?

563
53:12.100 --> 53:13.070
Fuen.

564
53:14.570 --> 53:17.300
It's not that I meant to keep it from you.

565
53:20.570 --> 53:23.230
I was waiting for your answer.

566
53:23.230 --> 53:24.930
What answer?

567
53:28.830 --> 53:29.930
Oh.

568
53:32.770 --> 53:34.070
If I don't lie to you,

569
53:34.530 --> 53:36.470
you'll leave me, right?

570
53:39.000 --> 53:41.130
Then just leave me.

571
53:57.170 --> 54:01.370
So what? Tell me what you want me to do.

572
54:06.900 --> 54:09.000
You really want an answer that badly?

573
54:12.730 --> 54:15.170
I don't want to see your face anymore.

574
54:15.670 --> 54:16.870
Go wherever you want.

575
54:17.430 --> 54:19.230
You're so damn selfish.

576
54:27.430 --> 54:30.270
If two people truly confess their love

577
54:30.270 --> 54:33.630
as the last firework is launched into the sky,

578
54:33.630 --> 54:38.370
they'll be blessed by the sacred spirits, just as they once were.

579
54:54.470 --> 54:57.300
I don't know what to do anymore.

580
54:58.470 --> 55:01.170
This is our whole life we're talking about.

581
55:25.630 --> 55:27.400
You're not alone, Mii.

582
55:28.230 --> 55:29.630
You still have me.

583
55:46.230 --> 55:49.930
Didn't you tell me to trust your actions?

584
55:59.770 --> 56:03.670
"Didn't you tell me to trust your actions?"

585
56:04.500 --> 56:07.670
If we talk in here, it's not cheating, right?

586
56:07.670 --> 56:09.370
But let me care for you better.

587
56:09.370 --> 56:11.170
This is our whole life.

588
56:11.170 --> 56:12.170
Go wherever you want.

589
56:13.030 --> 56:14.100
You're so damn selfish.

590
56:27.300 --> 56:31.670
"Din always came to my room. This time, I want to be the one to come to you." (Star)

591
56:31.670 --> 56:33.830
"What I want to say is about Rei. I have my reasons."

592
56:33.830 --> 56:36.370
"Long ago we made a deal that I'd stay with him and let him keep pursuing me..." (Star)

593
56:36.630 --> 56:37.870
"Because I know I can't be away from you. Having you by my side"

594
56:37.870 --> 56:39.000
"is what I'm used to. Even one day apart feels wrong."

595
56:39.000 --> 56:40.270
"That's how I knew I like you. Not Star... But what you just did"

596
56:40.270 --> 56:41.770
"was walk away, keep your distance, and you didn't even... give me time to prepare." (Fuen)

597
56:42.130 --> 56:43.030
My bad, Physics.

598
56:43.030 --> 56:44.800
But I love your brother like crazy.

599
56:44.800 --> 56:47.330
Do you know how hard you made my brother cry?

600
56:47.330 --> 56:48.900
Hey! Physics!

601
56:52.170 --> 56:53.300
I'm asking seriously.

602
56:53.300 --> 56:56.930
Did you ever care, or ever think about me at all?

603
56:56.930 --> 56:58.270
I've had enough

604
56:58.270 --> 56:59.530
of everything about you.

605
56:59.530 --> 57:01.070
I get that you're mad at me.

606
57:01.070 --> 57:03.300
But when you said you didn't want to see my face,

607
57:03.300 --> 57:04.300
I was lost.

608
57:04.300 --> 57:05.130
What about me?

609
57:05.130 --> 57:06.000
What's my score?

610
57:06.370 --> 57:08.100
I already answered that day.

611
57:08.700 --> 57:10.430
That day was that day.

612
57:10.430 --> 57:13.330
Today, I want to know how much of your heart I've won.
